UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 7, Week 2, Lesson 3: Dividing integers', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Division of integers undoes multiplication: magnitudes divide, signs follow the same rules as multiplication. Division by zero is undefined.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same method to a larger number or a new context, then compare two solution paths for accuracy.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nEvaluate (−20)÷5 and (−20)÷(−4); explain one using a multiplication check.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: −4 and 5; check multiplies back correctly.\n\nWATCH FOR\nWriting a number for division by zero. State undefined instead.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nSolve sixteen divisions including two undefined cases; prove eight answers with multiplication checks.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Mathematics","learning_intention":"Division of integers undoes multiplication: magnitudes divide, signs follow the same rules as multiplication. Division by zero is undefined.","lesson_number":3,"lesson_role":"Problem solving","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: place-value chart or number line"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["MA4-ARI-C-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Solve sixteen divisions including two undefined cases; prove eight answers with multiplication checks. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: Strong answer: −4 and 5; check multiplies back correctly. Reasoning: I used division by attending to inverse of multiply rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Writing a number for division by zero. State undefined instead. Correction: Strong answer: −4 and 5; check multiplies back correctly. Why: the correction restores accurate use of division.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Writing a number for division by zero. State undefined instead. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Solve one fresh problem that uses division with different numbers from the worked model. Show working and name the places or values that matter.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Describe one likely mistake with division, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require new numbers, visible working and named places/values. / Require a real misconception, corrected working and a method reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Strong answer: −4 and 5; check multiplies back correctly. This matches the lesson skill for division.","options":["Writing a number for division by zero. State undefined instead.","Ignore place value and read digits from left to right as ones only.","Copy the model numbers and call that independent work.","Strong answer: −4 and 5; check multiplies back correctly."],"question":"Evaluate (−20)÷5 and (−20)÷(−4); explain one using a multiplication check. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Writing a number for division by zero. State undefined instead. That misconception weakens accuracy; the other choices align with the lesson idea.","options":["Writing a number for division by zero. State undefined instead.","Division of integers undoes multiplication: magnitudes divide, signs follow the same rul